1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,557
What would you say, if they threw you into a fire? He said: Allah is enough for us.

2
00:00:07,607 --> 00:00:11,363
They threw him into a blazing furnace. His crime?

3
00:00:11,413 --> 00:00:16,568
He told them: your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth...

4
00:00:16,618 --> 00:00:18,530
and he broke their idols.

5
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:24,970
But Allah said: "O fire, be coolness and safety upon Ibrahim."

6
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:31,340
Who was this man, who stood alone against his father, his people, and a king?

7
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:40,697
Long ago, among a people devoted to statues, there lived a young man named Ibrahim, alayhis salaam.

8
00:00:40,747 --> 00:00:46,141
His people carved statues with their own hands, and stayed devoted to them.

9
00:00:46,191 --> 00:00:51,270
They called on them, hoping they would help, fearing they would harm.

10
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:55,830
And his own father, Azar, worshipped them too.

11
00:00:55,880 --> 00:01:04,883
But the young man looked at the idols, and saw what they were: carved things that could not hear, and could not see.

12
00:01:04,933 --> 00:01:09,366
One day he said to his father: "Do you take idols as gods?

13
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:13,430
Indeed, I see you and your people in clear error."

14
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,391
It was a dangerous thing to say.

15
00:01:15,441 --> 00:01:21,210
These idols were the way of their fathers, and the bond that held the whole people together.

16
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:26,960
But Allah had given this young man his sound judgement, and a sound heart.

17
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:38,110
Allah showed Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, the realm of the heavens and the earth, and gave him an argument against his people, step by step.

18
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:43,604
When the night grew dark, he saw a star, and said: this is my lord.

19
00:01:43,654 --> 00:01:48,930
But when it set, he said: "I do not love those that disappear."

20
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:53,653
Then he saw the moon rising, and said: this is my lord.

21
00:01:53,703 --> 00:02:02,130
But when it set, he said: unless my Lord guides me, I will surely be among those who go astray.

22
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:07,543
Then he saw the sun rising. This is my lord, he said, this is greater.

23
00:02:07,593 --> 00:02:11,690
But when it set, he turned to his people and said:

24
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:18,050
O my people, I am free from all that you associate with Allah.

25
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:29,010
"Indeed, I have turned my face toward He who created the heavens and the earth, inclining toward truth, and I am not of those who associate others with Allah."

26
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:35,005
Everything that rises... sets. Only the One who made them never disappears.

27
00:02:35,055 --> 00:02:41,610
But saying this aloud... was about to cost him his home, and nearly his life.

28
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:45,950
The hardest call of all was to his own father.

29
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,736
And listen to how gently he spoke.

30
00:02:48,786 --> 00:02:57,790
"O my father, why do you worship that which does not hear, and does not see, and will not benefit you at all?"

31
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:02,587
O my father, knowledge has come to me that has not come to you.

32
00:03:02,637 --> 00:03:06,577
So follow me, and I will guide you to an even path.

33
00:03:06,627 --> 00:03:08,324
O my father, do not worship Satan.

34
00:03:08,374 --> 00:03:11,590
Indeed Satan has ever been, to the Most Merciful, disobedient.

35
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:17,471
O my father, I fear that a punishment from the Most Merciful will touch you.

36
00:03:17,521 --> 00:03:22,031
Four times he called him: O my father. Every word, gentle.

37
00:03:22,081 --> 00:03:27,167
But his father answered: "Have you no desire for my gods, O Ibrahim?

38
00:03:27,217 --> 00:03:32,971
If you do not stop, I will surely stone you. So leave me, for a long time."

39
00:03:33,021 --> 00:03:36,574
And Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said: "Peace be upon you.

40
00:03:36,624 --> 00:03:42,361
I will ask forgiveness for you from my Lord. Indeed, He is ever gracious to me."

41
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:48,037
Words had not moved them. So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, made a plan.

42
00:03:48,087 --> 00:03:59,878
He asked his people: "What are these statues to which you are devoted?" They said: we found our fathers worshipping them.

43
00:03:59,928 --> 00:04:04,445
He said: you and your fathers have been in clear error.

44
00:04:04,495 --> 00:04:11,291
And he swore: by Allah, I will plan against your idols after you turn your backs.

45
00:04:11,341 --> 00:04:18,480
He cast a look at the stars, and said: I am ill. So they turned away from him, and left.

46
00:04:18,530 --> 00:04:22,998
And Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, went to their gods alone.

47
00:04:23,048 --> 00:04:27,671
He broke the idols into pieces, all of them... except the biggest one.

48
00:04:27,721 --> 00:04:32,799
When the people returned, they cried: who has done this to our gods?

49
00:04:32,849 --> 00:04:38,011
Some said: we heard a young man speak of them. His name is Ibrahim.

50
00:04:38,061 --> 00:04:44,781
They brought him before everyone and asked: did you do this to our gods, O Ibrahim?

51
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:52,624
He said: "Rather, this one, the biggest of them, did it. So ask them, if they can speak."

52
00:04:52,674 --> 00:04:56,800
For a moment, they turned on themselves: you are the wrongdoers!

53
00:04:56,850 --> 00:05:01,771
Then they turned back, and said: you know very well that these do not speak.

54
00:05:01,821 --> 00:05:09,962
And he said: then do you worship, instead of Allah, what can neither benefit you nor harm you?

55
00:05:10,012 --> 00:05:15,901
Shame on you, and on what you worship. Will you not use reason?

56
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:20,770
They had lost the argument. So they turned to force.

57
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:26,430
"Burn him, and support your gods, if you are to act."

58
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:32,563
They said: build for him a furnace, and throw him into the blazing fire.

59
00:05:32,613 --> 00:05:36,280
A young man, alone, falling into the flames.

60
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:44,630
And then Allah gave the fire a single command: "O fire, be coolness and safety upon Ibrahim."

61
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:48,629
The fire that was made to burn... obeyed its Creator.

62
00:05:48,679 --> 00:05:55,947
And as they threw him, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, had said: حَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيْلُ.

63
00:05:55,997 --> 00:06:00,010
Allah is enough for us, and He is the best Guardian.

64
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:05,650
"And they intended for him harm, but We made them the greatest losers."

65
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:13,000
But the fire was not his hardest test. That one would come years later... in a dream.

66
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:17,510
There was a king to whom Allah had given a kingdom.

67
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:23,660
And because Allah had given him a kingdom, he argued with Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, about his Lord.

68
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:30,050
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said: my Lord is the One who gives life and causes death.

69
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:34,100
The king said: I give life and cause death.

70
00:06:34,513 --> 00:06:42,030
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said: "Indeed, Allah brings up the sun from the east, so bring it up from the west."

71
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:47,846
And the disbeliever was overwhelmed. A king, with all his kingdom...

72
00:06:47,896 --> 00:06:54,540
silenced by one sentence. And Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.

73
00:06:55,440 --> 00:07:01,960
His father had threatened to stone him. His people had tried to burn him.

74
00:07:02,010 --> 00:07:05,250
A king had argued against his Lord.

75
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:10,398
And one man believed in him: Lut, alayhis salaam.

76
00:07:10,448 --> 00:07:20,483
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, left his people, and Allah brought him and Lut to a land He had blessed.

77
00:07:20,533 --> 00:07:25,603
He said: "Indeed, I will go to my Lord. He will guide me."

78
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:34,650
He said: I will leave you and what you worship besides Allah, and I will call upon my Lord.

79
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:42,590
And as he grew older, he made one more dua: "My Lord, grant me a child from among the righteous."

80
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,560
And Allah gave him good news: a forbearing boy.

81
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:51,414
His son Ismail, alayhis salaam, was born.

82
00:07:51,464 --> 00:07:55,620
And then came a test that no father would choose.

83
00:07:55,670 --> 00:08:05,882
By Allah's command, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, brought the baby and his mother to a dry valley, with no water, no plants, and no people.

84
00:08:05,932 --> 00:08:07,650
The valley of Makkah.

85
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:12,534
He left them there, with a bag of dates and a skin of water.

86
00:08:12,584 --> 00:08:19,291
As he walked away, the mother called after him: has Allah commanded you to do this?

87
00:08:19,341 --> 00:08:23,970
He said: yes. And she said: then He will not neglect us.

88
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:42,510
Out of their sight, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, faced the House, raised his hands, and prayed: "Our Lord, I have settled some of my descendants in an uncultivated valley near Your sacred House, that they may establish prayer."

89
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:52,140
When the water ran out, the mother ran between two hills, Safa and Marwa, seven times, searching for any sign of help.

90
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:58,841
Then she heard a voice. At the place of Zamzam, the ground was struck, and water flowed.

91
00:08:58,891 --> 00:09:02,530
The spring of Zamzam. It is still flowing today.

92
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:11,370
Every pilgrim who walks between Safa and Marwa is walking in the footsteps of a mother who trusted Allah.

93
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:16,260
And that baby would grow up... to become the son in his father's dream.

94
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:22,067
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, had seen the fire turn cool.

95
00:09:22,117 --> 00:09:30,290
He had seen his Lord answer his duas. And still, he asked his Lord for one more thing.

96
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:35,690
"My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead."

97
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:39,173
Allah said: have you not believed?

98
00:09:39,223 --> 00:09:45,030
He said: "Yes, but only that my heart may be satisfied."

99
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:50,557
So Allah told him: take four birds, and draw them close to you.

100
00:09:50,607 --> 00:09:55,537
Then put a portion of them on each hill. Then call them.

101
00:09:55,587 --> 00:10:00,979
Call them, Allah said, and they will come to you in haste.

102
00:10:01,029 --> 00:10:05,803
And know that Allah is Exalted in Might, and Wise.

103
00:10:05,853 --> 00:10:12,040
Faith does not mean you never ask. It means you ask the One who has the answer.

104
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,074
Years passed.

105
00:10:16,124 --> 00:10:22,550
Ismail, alayhis salaam, grew into a boy who could walk and work beside his father.

106
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:25,298
Then Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, saw a dream.

107
00:10:25,348 --> 00:10:28,597
And his son understood it as a command from Allah.

108
00:10:28,647 --> 00:10:34,015
He said: "O my son, indeed I have seen in a dream that I sacrifice you.

109
00:10:34,065 --> 00:10:36,090
So see what you think."

110
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:41,447
And the son answered: "O my father, do as you are commanded.

111
00:10:41,497 --> 00:10:46,130
You will find me, if Allah wills, of the steadfast."

112
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:53,420
When they had both submitted, and Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, laid him down on his forehead...

113
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:59,171
Allah called to him: O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision.

114
00:10:59,221 --> 00:11:03,250
And Allah says: indeed, this was the clear trial.

115
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:08,370
"And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice."

116
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:16,660
Every Eid al-Adha, Muslims remember this moment: a father and a son who both submitted to Allah.

117
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:20,893
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, was now an old man.

118
00:11:20,943 --> 00:11:25,457
And his wife, Sarah, alayhas salaam, had never had a child.

119
00:11:25,507 --> 00:11:33,721
One day, guests entered upon him. Strangers, a people unknown. They said: peace.

120
00:11:33,771 --> 00:11:35,430
He said: peace.

121
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:38,581
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, did not delay.

122
00:11:38,631 --> 00:11:43,537
He went to his family, and came back with a fat roasted calf.

123
00:11:43,587 --> 00:11:50,409
He placed it near them and said: "Will you not eat?" But their hands did not reach for it.

124
00:11:50,459 --> 00:11:52,497
And he felt afraid of them.

125
00:11:52,547 --> 00:11:57,030
They said: do not fear. We are messengers, sent to the people of Lut.

126
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,977
And they gave him good news.

127
00:11:59,027 --> 00:12:02,074
His wife, who was standing nearby, smiled.

128
00:12:02,124 --> 00:12:08,830
And they gave her the good news of a son, Ishaq, and after Ishaq, Yaqub, alayhimus salaam.

129
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:14,761
She said: shall I give birth, when I am an old woman, and my husband is an old man?

130
00:12:14,811 --> 00:12:20,191
This is an amazing thing! They said: "Are you amazed at the decree of Allah?

131
00:12:20,241 --> 00:12:25,640
May the mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, people of the house."

132
00:12:25,690 --> 00:12:31,606
From Ismail, alayhis salaam, would come the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him.

133
00:12:31,656 --> 00:12:39,137
From Ishaq, alayhis salaam, would come Yaqub, Yusuf, Musa, Dawud, Sulaiman and Isa, alayhimus salaam.

134
00:12:39,187 --> 00:12:44,360
And Allah placed prophethood and the Book among his descendants.

135
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:50,569
Then Allah showed Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, the place of His House.

136
00:12:50,619 --> 00:12:53,350
And father and son began to build.

137
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:59,682
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, laid the stones. Ismail, alayhis salaam, carried them.

138
00:12:59,732 --> 00:13:03,770
And as the walls of the Kaaba rose, they prayed:

139
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:11,050
"Our Lord, accept this from us. Indeed, You are the Hearing, the Knowing."

140
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:19,025
Our Lord, make us Muslims to You, and from our descendants a Muslim nation.

141
00:13:19,075 --> 00:13:23,950
Show us our rites, and accept our repentance.

142
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:34,626
And they asked for one more thing: our Lord, send among them a messenger from themselves, who will recite Your verses to them.

143
00:13:34,676 --> 00:13:40,971
Long after, Allah answered that dua: Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him.

144
00:13:41,021 --> 00:13:45,112
Then Allah commanded: "Proclaim to the people the Hajj.

145
00:13:45,162 --> 00:13:51,661
They will come to you on foot, and on every lean camel, from every distant pass."

146
00:13:51,821 --> 00:13:59,501
And they still come. Millions every year, just as Allah promised Ibrahim, alayhis salaam.

147
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:11,550
In his old age, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, stood in the valley that had once been empty, and he made a dua that Muslims still recite today.

148
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:18,310
"My Lord, make this city secure, and keep me and my sons away from worshipping idols."

149
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:23,859
Praise be to Allah, who gave me in my old age Ismail and Ishaq.

150
00:14:23,909 --> 00:14:27,990
Indeed, my Lord is the Hearer of supplication.

151
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:34,082
"My Lord, make me one who establishes prayer, and from my descendants too.

152
00:14:34,132 --> 00:14:36,537
Our Lord, and accept my dua."

153
00:14:36,587 --> 00:14:45,090
"Our Lord, forgive me, and my parents, and the believers, on the Day the account is established."

154
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:47,783
And Muslims still make this dua today.

155
00:14:47,833 --> 00:14:53,760
The words of Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, kept in the Quran, still on our tongues.

156
00:14:54,660 --> 00:14:58,385
A young man among idols who would not bow.

157
00:14:58,435 --> 00:15:05,487
A son who spoke gently to a father who threatened him. A young man in the fire.

158
00:15:05,537 --> 00:15:07,734
A father in a dry valley.

159
00:15:07,784 --> 00:15:13,783
A father and son raising the foundations of a House for all people.

160
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:19,870
Every time, he turned to Allah. And every time, Allah was enough for him.

161
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:25,150
Allah says: "There has already been for you an excellent pattern in Abraham and those with him."

162
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:36,786
And Allah kept his name with ours: every time we send blessings on the Prophet, peace be upon him, as he taught us, we name Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim.

163
00:15:36,836 --> 00:15:38,903
"Peace upon Ibrahim."

164
00:15:38,953 --> 00:15:47,879
So when you feel alone, say what he said as they threw him into the fire: حَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيْلُ.

165
00:15:47,929 --> 00:15:52,130
Allah is enough for us, and He is the best Guardian.

166
00:15:52,180 --> 00:15:56,721
Which moment of his story moved you most? Tell us in the comments.

167
00:15:56,771 --> 00:16:02,495
And watch the full movies of Prophet Musa and Prophet Sulaiman, alayhimas salaam...

168
00:16:02,545 --> 00:16:03,380
links below.
